# Hushbringer stops creatures entering or dying from causing triggers, and nothing else (CR 603.2). Bot1's Badgermole Cub
# earthbends its Forest; Bot2's Hushbringer arrives; on turn 4 Bot2 exiles the creature land with Swords to Plowshares.
# Being exiled is not dying (CR 700.4), so "When this land dies or is put into exile, return it to the battlefield tapped"
# triggers and the Forest comes back, tapped and a land only, and Bot1 gains 1 life for its power. The returning Forest is
# not a creature, so its entering is not stopped either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Badgermole Cub
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Hushbringer
Swords to Plowshares
Plains x10

